      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The initial TiVNbTa alloy has a dendritic microstructure.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The initial TiVNbTa alloy has a lower-temperature yield strength of approximately 800 MPa.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "At 1273 K, the baseline TiVNbTa alloy has a yield strength of 330 MPa.",
      "field": "baseline",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "At 1273 K and 30% strain, the baseline TiVNbTa alloy has a compressive strength of 423 MPa.",
      "field": "baseline",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed intervention is addition of approximately 1–2 at% carbon during vacuum arc melting.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Carbon addition followed by aging will produce uniformly dispersed nanoscale carbide precipitates, such as TiC, in the BCC TiVNbTa matrix.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The carbon-induced carbide precipitates will be stable at approximately 1273 K.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC5627260::web::001::introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Carbide precipitates will impede dislocation motion at elevated temperature through precipitation strengthening.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC5627260::web::001::introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Precipitation strengthening can improve the elevated-temperature strength of otherwise single-phase HEAs.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC5627260::web::001::introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Carbon modification will raise the TiVNbTa yield strength at 1273 K significantly above the 330 MPa baseline.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC5627260::web::001::introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The carbide-strengthened alloy will maintain structural integrity during prolonged high-temperature exposure.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC5627260::web::001::introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "A strain rate near 10^-3 s^-1 is used in elevated-temperature mechanical testing of refractory HEAs.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10453588::web::004::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Testing at 1273 K, up to 30% tensile or compressive strain, and near 10^-3 s^-1 represents typical service loading for a W/TiVNbTa/CuCrZr intermediate heat-transfer layer.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The magnitude of strengthening depends on precipitate uniformity and volume fraction.",
      "field": "uncertainty",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC5627260::web::001::introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Carbon addition and carbide formation may embrittle the TiVNbTa alloy.",
      "field": "uncertainty",
